{
  "chapter": "durability/compensation",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "Durable execution fixed the crash, the retry and the duplicate. It does not fix a",
    "sequence where every step succeeded and the outcome is still wrong.",
    "Compensation is not rollback. A refund creates a second ledger entry rather than deleting",
    "the first: the business effect reverses and the history stays.",
    "In a saga the sequence is designed; in an agent the model chose it. So compensations",
    "attach to tools in the catalogue rather than to steps in a workflow, and a write with no",
    "declared compensation cannot take part.",
    "Order by reversibility and name the pivot: everything fallible before it, everything",
    "irreversible after it. Past the pivot the correct response to failure is to finish.",
    "Unwind in reverse, over only what actually succeeded, and let one failed compensation",
    "raise an incident without stopping the others.",
    "Mark business rejections non-retryable so the saga starts unwinding immediately instead",
    "of burning its retry budget first."
  ],
